From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LNPANDY <lnp-andy@hotmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 13:55:24 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] iOS: isolate DmShellGame Objective-C classes and restrict
 exported symbols

Objective-C class registration is process-global and ignores RTLD_LOCAL, so
loading multiple DmShellGame frameworks (across different titles or chained
NRO frameworks) inside DmShell caused duplicate class collisions and method
dispatch cross-talk across ~41 engine Objective-C classes and Swift modules.

Add dm/ios/tools/gen_objc_namespace.py to lexically scan engine sources for
project-owned Objective-C @implementation definitions while ignoring
categories, comments, string literals, macOS-only files and host shell
sources. Emit Gen/framework/objc_namespace.h with per-framework DmFw_<tag>_*
class macros (distinguishing both title IDs and chain suffixes) together
with Gen/framework/exported_symbols.txt matching the shell dlsym contract.

Wire DmShellGame in project-framework.yml and build_ipa.sh to force-include
objc_namespace.h in C, Objective-C and Swift compilation, set a unique
PRODUCT_MODULE_NAME per framework, and pass -exported_symbols_list to the
linker. Replace the string-literal lookup NSClassFromString(@"DmTVSceneDelegate")
in front_ios.m with DmTVSceneDelegate.class so the scene delegate follows
the namespace macro. Extend compile_check.py, test_framework_link.py and a
new dual-dylib dlopen test suite in test_objc_namespace.py.

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: Isolate per-framework Objective-C/Swift runtime classes and global symbol exports in the iOS shared shell
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#451
